# Appendix C Master Index of Formalized Lean 4 Theorems and Open Problems {#appendix-c-master-index-of-formalized-lean-4-theorems-and-open-problems}

This appendix serves as the **Master Audit Ledger** of the epistemic boundaries governing this monograph. Under the Prelude's contract, Lean verification, written proofs, and open problems declare their evidence separately. Sections C.1–C.3 audit the frozen declarations in `trureturing.lock.json` at the pinned `trureturing@dev` commit [{commit}](trureturing:); C.4 lists open problems and selected literature boundaries:

1. **C.1 Frozen Theorem Index ({{T}} Unique `theorem` Declarations)**: This section contains every locked declaration of kind `theorem` cited by `lean="<GID>"` on at least one `:::` environment header in the Chinese edition. Each citation must resolve to a kernel-verified, frozen theorem at the pinned commit.
2. **C.2 Formal Definition and Carrier Index ({{D}} Unique Declarations: {{D_def}} `def` + {{inductive}} `inductive`)**: Definitions and inductive types cited by `lean=` on Chinese environment headers; **C.3 Inline Auxiliary Theorems and Definitions ({{R}} Declarations: {{R_theorem}} `theorem` + {{R_def}} `def`)** contains the remaining declarations, which no environment header cites. The three disjoint sections cover all **{{total}} unique declarations** in `trureturing.lock.json` (${{T}} + {{D}} + {{R}} = {{total}}$). Media consumers are listed separately at the end of each row and do not determine the partition.
3. **C.4 Open Problems and Literature Boundary Register (11 Entries: 6 `conjecture` + 3 `problem` Environments + 2 Literature `remark` Boundaries)**: None of the nine open environments carries a `lean` attribute; the other two entries are explicitly attributed external literature boundaries and are excluded from the count of verified declarations.

Section 16.3's [@thm-central-defect-endpoint-average] and its [written proof](ch16-qsvt-walks-and-compilation.md#pf-central-defect-endpoint-average) are neither frozen declarations nor open problems. Their DOI, source locator, and [formalization request #10](https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing-requests/issues/10) appear in the text and the automatically generated written-proof ledger. They add nothing to the locked-declaration totals, green charts, or C.4 counts above.

::: {.viz src="lean-declaration-map" preset="all" height="500"}
**{{total}} cells, one for each locked declaration.** The timeline runs from the Prelude to Appendix E, with Appendix C itself excluded as a landing column. Each declaration lands in the first unit that cites it: {{theorems}} cells are theorems and {{definitions}} are definitions or inductive types; {{env}} filled cells are cited by `lean=` on environment headers, while {{R}} hollow cells appear only inline. Each declaration occupies one cell regardless of reuse. The C.1 chart below instead counts only the theorems cited by each chapter’s environment headers, counting them again in different chapters.
:::

---

