## C.4 Open Conjectures and Unformalized Problems (11 Entries: 6 Conjectures + 3 Open Problems + 2 Literature Boundaries — Zero `lean` Attributes) {#sec-appendix-c-open-register}

::: {.remark #rem-appendix-c-open-literature-register title="Register of Open Conjectures and External Literature Boundaries (Literature Result, Not Formalized in This Book)"}
**Literature result, not formalized in this book (only for external literature boundary entries `O6` and `O7` below; `O1`–`O5` and `O8` are `conjecture` environments, while `O9`–`O11` are `problem` environments).** The book contains nine open environments, all without a `lean` attribute. Open conjectures, open problems and classical literature results are identified separately and excluded from the count of verified declarations.

| # | Environment Anchor ID | Chapter | Conjecture / Frontier Problem Title | Core Mathematical or Physical Statement Summary | `lean` Attribute | Badge Status |
| :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: |
| O1 | `#conj-complexity-equals-volume` | `CH20` | Complexity Equals Volume (CV Conjecture, Susskind) | Maximal interior spatial slice volume $V(t)$ of an asymptotic AdS black hole scales proportionally to boundary state circuit complexity $\mathcal{C}(t) \sim V(t)/(G_N \ell_{\mathrm{AdS}})$ | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O2 | `#conj-er-equals-epr` | `CH20` | $\mathrm{ER}=\mathrm{EPR}$ Wormhole–Entanglement Duality (Maldacena–Susskind) | Non-traversable Einstein–Rosen bridges (ER wormholes) in bulk gravity are geometrically dual to maximally entangled EPR pairs in non-perturbative quantum gravity | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O3 | `#conj-p-neq-np` | `CH20` (cited in `CH30` / Coda) | $\mathrm{P} \neq \mathrm{NP}$ Complexity Separation Conjecture | Under the standard uniform Turing-machine computational model over a finite alphabet, there exists a formal language in $\mathrm{NP}$ that does not belong to $\mathrm{P}$ ($\mathrm{P} \neq \mathrm{NP}$) | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O4 | `#conj-riemann-hypothesis` | `CH22` | The Riemann Hypothesis | Every nontrivial zero of the Riemann zeta function $\zeta(s)$ lies on the critical symmetry line $\operatorname{Re}(s) = 1/2$ | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O5 | `#conj-schanuel-dottie` | `CH24` | Schanuel's Conjecture Applied to the Algebraic Independence of $\theta^*$ and $\pi$ | Schanuel's conjecture implies that the self-referential Dottie root $\theta^* = \cos\theta^*$ and $\pi$ are algebraically independent over $\mathbb{Q}$ ($\operatorname{tr.deg}_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}(\theta^*, \pi) = 2$; Chow's conditional result $\theta^* \notin \mathrm{EL}$ is noted separately in `#rem-banach-dottie-hairy-ball-literature`) | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O6 | `#rem-ryu-takayanagi-literature` | `CH19` | Continuous AdS/CFT Ryu–Takayanagi Minimal-Surface Formula | Full continuum gravitational path-integral derivation of $S(A) = \operatorname{Area}(\gamma_A)/(4G_N)$ (this book formalizes only the discrete `BridgeGraph` quantum max-flow min-cut theorem) | None (Literature) | `Literature` |
| O7 | `#rem-diophantine-z-in-q-literature` | `CH23` | Hilbert's Tenth Problem over $\mathbb{Q}$ ($H_{10}(\mathbb{Q})$) & Existential Definability of $\mathbb{Z} \subset \mathbb{Q}$ | Whether $\mathbb{Z}$ admits a purely existential ($\exists$) Diophantine definition in $\mathbb{Q}$ and whether $H_{10}(\mathbb{Q})$ is decidable (Koenigsmann 2016 proved a $\forall\exists$ first-order characterization, while $H_{10}(\mathbb{Q})$ remains open) | None (Literature) | `OPEN / Lit.` |
| O8 | `#conj-coda-navier-stokes-regularity` | `CH30` | Unforced 3D Incompressible Navier–Stokes Global Regularity Conjecture (Clay Millennium Statements A / B) | For strictly positive viscosity $\nu > 0$ and identically zero external force $\mathbf{f} \equiv \mathbf{0}$, whether every smooth divergence-free rapidly decaying (on $\mathbb{R}^3$) or periodic (on $\mathbb{T}^3$) initial velocity $\mathbf{u}_0$ admits a global smooth finite-energy solution on $[0, \infty)$ or develops finite-time blow-up (OpenAI's forced C / D result follows an accepted route in the official problem; see [@rem-ch30-navier-stokes-forced-literature] for external literature and its published formalization, outside this book's frozen theorems) | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O9 | `#prob-ch39-p2e-fractal-horizon` | `CH39` | Rauzy Fractal-Horizon Entanglement Scaling in Pisot Cut-and-Project Quantum Many-Body Systems | For $K \ge 3$ Pisot cut-and-project systems, can a rigorously constructed family of local gapped ground states or encoded states have asymptotic entanglement governed by the internal Rauzy boundary dimension $D_F$, such as $S_{\mathrm{ent}}(R) \asymp R^{D_F}$ or a fractal correction, with spectral-gap and locality criteria for preserving or violating the usual codimension-one area law? Finite encoding and null-boundary theorems do not prove this physical scaling | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O10 | `#prob-appendix-d-time-horizon` | Appendix D | Unified Dynamics for Covariant State Reduction, Emergent Clocks and Evaporating-Horizon Unitarity | Construct measurement dynamics without privileged Lorentz foliations or external clocks, derive the thermodynamic arrow from the Wheeler–DeWitt constraint, and reconcile late Page purification of Hawking radiation with smooth near-horizon vacuum entanglement (AMPS); finite-dimensional entropy and finite-arena escape theorems provide local algebraic analogies only | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |
| O11 | `#prob-monitored-spectral-mean` | `CH07` | Formalization Gap from Monitored Return Histories to Occupied Spectral Cardinality (Grünbaum–Velázquez–Werner–Werner Theorem 2) | For any finite-dimensional complex inner-product space, unitary $U$, and unit vector $v$ with monitored first-return probabilities $p_{n+1} = \lvert\langle v, U T^n v\rangle\rvert^2$ and occupied spectrum $S = \{\lambda \in \mathbb{C} : \exists w \in E,\; Uw = \lambda w \text{ and } \langle w, v\rangle \neq 0\}$, formalize that $\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} p_{n+1} = 1$ implies $S$ is finite and $\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}(n+1)p_{n+1} = \#S$ (a formalization gap for a known literature theorem, not an unsolved mathematical conjecture) | None (Forbidden) | `OPEN` (Red) |

:::

