## C.5 Pinned Commit & Kernel Integrity Checklist {#sec-appendix-c-integrity-checklist}

Every build and release of this book mechanically enforces the following five verification gates via `./tbook pin` and `./tbook check`:

| Verification Gate | Target Parameter / Contract Value | Toolchain Mechanism | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| **Upstream Repository & Branch** | `the-omega-institute/trureturing` branch `dev` | `site.toml` `[trureturing]` config & `git merge-base --is-ancestor` check | `PASS` |
| **Pinned Commit SHA** | [{commit}](trureturing:) | Locked in `trureturing.lock.json` `commit` field | `PASS` |
| **Frozen Theorem Count** | `{{T}}` environment-cited theorems (`{{theorems}}` total entries of `kind == "theorem"` including inline references) | Verified against `Golden/Frozen/state/<module>.lean.json` state slices and `statement_id` digests | `PASS` |
| **Auxiliary Definition / Structure Count** | `{{D}}` environment-cited definitions/inductive types; `{{definitions}}` in total (`{{defs}}` `def` + `{{inductive}}` `inductive`) including inline references | Kept in C.2 and never counted as `theorem / lemma / proposition / corollary` boxes | `PASS` |
| **Bilingual Structural Alignment** | 100% parity between `zh` and `en` chapter order, env IDs, and Lean citations | Checked item-by-item by `./tbook check` (`0 error(s)`) | `PASS` |

::: {.figure src="appc-ledger"}
**The ledger of the ${{total}}$ locked declarations: kind × citation mode.** Rows are theorems and definitions; columns are environment-header `lean=` citations, inline text with media consumers, and inline links alone. The theorem row is ${{T}} + {{thm_media}} + {{thm_inline}} = {{theorems}}$ and the definition row ${{D}} + {{def_media}} + {{R_def}} = {{definitions}}$. Dashed frames follow the environment-based indexes: C.1 $= {{T}}$, C.2 $= {{D}}$, C.3 $= {{thm_media}} + {{thm_inline}} + {{def_media}} + {{R_def}} = {{R}}$. Media consumers do not change the index partition.
:::

The first row of this ledger is the ${{theorems}}$ green cells of the declaration map: the ${{T}}$ cited on environment headers are filled, the other ${{thm_media}} + {{thm_inline}} = {{R_theorem}}$ hollow.

::: {.viz src="lean-declaration-map" preset="theorems" height="500"}
**Theorems only.** The map keeps the {{theorems}} locked entries of kind `theorem`: {{T}} filled cells cited by `lean=` on environment headers and {{R_theorem}} hollow cells appearing only in inline links in the Chinese text.
:::

::: {.remark #rem-appendix-c-epistemic-boundary title="Verification Boundary Note for the Complete Declaration Index"}
The {{T}} environment-cited theorems in C.1, {{D}} environment-cited definitions/inductive types in C.2, and {{R}} inline declarations in C.3 form a disjoint cover of all {{total}} entries in `trureturing.lock.json` ({{theorems}} `theorem` + {{defs}} `def` + 10 `inductive`). Source links resolve at the pinned `trureturing@dev` commit [{commit}](trureturing:). The nine open environments and two literature boundaries in C.4 are excluded from those locked declarations; index membership, explanatory prose and kernel proof have distinct roles.
:::

